Package: didml
Title: Difference-in-Differences with Machine Learning
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Andres", "Mena", email = "andres_mena@brown.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
  )
Description: Unified estimation for difference-in-differences designs
    with machine learning nuisance estimation. Supports sharp DID
    (Sant'Anna & Zhao 2020 via DRDID, and DML-DID of Chang 2020),
    fuzzy DID (DML-Wald and DML-TC of Mena 2026), and extensible
    multi-period designs. Cross-fitted nuisance estimation via Lasso,
    Random Forest, neural networks, OLS, or user-supplied learners.
    Includes optimal propensity score trimming, clustered standard
    errors, and a bundled empirical application to the INPRES school
    construction program.
